# Sentinel file for .github/workflows/migrate-production-secrets.yml.
#
# Path-only trigger: pushing any change to this file on branch release-0-7-0
# fires the workflow, but the migration job only runs when the commit message
# contains the marker [run-migrate-prod-secrets].
#
# Touching this file in a normal commit (no marker) is a no-op for the
# migration and is the expected way to land the trigger implementation itself
# without firing a live migration. To execute a live migration, push a commit
# that modifies this file and includes the marker in its message.
#
# 2026-09-27: live-mutation sentinel update — fires the production migration.
# The trigger implementation (#38 / 919bbeb) was merged without this marker,
# so the migration workflow correctly skipped at step 1. This commit supplies
# the marker in the commit message to fire the actual production import.
#
# 2026-09-27 v2: importer fix landed via #39 (commit 4760482), which replaced
# the broken `KEY=@file` syntax with `infisical secrets set --file`. The
# first live sentinel push (commit 9747a16) ran against the broken importer
# and produced 5 garbage values (`@/tmp/...` literal paths). Those garbage
# values have been deleted (export now returns `[]`); this touch supplies the
# canonical marker to fire the production import with the fixed importer.
